    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d684-a1">

                <pb facs="0557" n="475" xml:id="pg475"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Attorney General to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-04-26"><hi rendition="#italic">April 26,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 90755–780.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to hand you a copy of a letter<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d684-f1"/> just received from the United States attorney for
                    the Territory of Arizona, replying to a communication from this Department,
                    transmitting to him a copy of a note from the Mexican embassy, stating that the
                    governor of Sonora had reported that armed bands had invaded that State from its
                    northern boundary, and requesting that steps be taken to prevent such
                    expedition.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. W.
                    Wickersham.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
